[{"category":"section","location":"benchmark/#Benchmark-Results","page":"Benchmark Results","text":"","title":"Benchmark Results"},{"category":"section","location":"benchmark/#Sweep-Heatmaps","page":"Benchmark Results","text":"We study how the cost of evaluating the semidiscrete right-hand side varies with the polynomial degree p and the refinement level L. Each case is examined along two lines through this plane: a level sweep, which refines the mesh at a fixed degree p = 3, and a degree sweep, which raises p on a fixed mesh with L = 12 in 1D, L = 6 in 2D, and L = 4 in 3D.\n\nAt every point, the target revision is compared with its baseline. Both revisions are measured in three alternating processes, and the speedup is defined as the median ratio of their process medians. Its uncertainty is quantified by a 95% two-level bootstrap interval, which accounts for variation both within and between processes.\n\nA change is reported only when it exceeds the noise band of ±3%, the range a speedup can reach through measurement noise alone. This band was calibrated with runs that compare identical code. A cell is shown in green when its entire interval lies above the band, in red when it lies below, and in white when it lies within. Hatched cells mark inconclusive results, whose intervals cross an edge of the band. Hovering over a cell reveals its details.\n\n<div id=\"sweep-heatmaps\"></div>","title":"Sweep Heatmaps"},{"category":"section","location":"#TrixiCUDA.jl","page":"Home","text":"TrixiCUDA.jl provides high-order DG solvers for hyperbolic PDEs with native CUDA.jl kernels.","title":"TrixiCUDA.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Performance-Benchmarks","page":"Home","text":"Performance is tracked by benchmarking TrixiCUDA.rhs_hyperbolic!, the evaluation of the semidiscrete right-hand side, in Float64 on the initial mesh of each case. All cases are adapted from Trixi.jl or TrixiShallowWater.jl examples on TreeMesh. The cases are selected so that every right-hand-side code path in each spatial dimension is covered by two to three cases, or by the only available example where no second one exists.","title":"Performance Benchmarks"},{"category":"section","location":"#Feature-Coverage","page":"Home","text":"The table lists, for each spatial dimension, how many of the 37 benchmark cases exercise each right-hand-side code path.\n\nCategory Feature 1D 2D 3D\nVolume integral Weak form 2 3 3\n Flux differencing 3 2 2\n Flux differencing, nonconservative 3 3 3\n Shock capturing 3 3 2\n Shock capturing, nonconservative 2 2 1 †\nBoundaries Non-periodic 2 2 2\n Non-periodic, nonconservative 2 1 † n/a\nMesh Mortars n/a 2 2\n Mortars, nonconservative n/a 1 † 1 †\nSources Source terms 3 3 2\nTotal  13 cases 13 cases 11 cases\n\nnote: Coverage limits\n† Covered by a single case because only one suitable TreeMesh example exists in Trixi.jl or TrixiShallowwater.jl.n/a: Mortars do not occur in 1D, and in 3D the boundary flux uses the same code path for conservative and nonconservative equations.","title":"Feature Coverage"},{"category":"section","location":"#Cases-by-Dimension","page":"Home","text":"The tables below list the individual cases behind the coverage summary, grouped by spatial dimension. For each case, they give the equation system, the right-hand-side features it exercises, and the Trixi.jl or TrixiShallowWater.jl example it is adapted from.\n\nCase is the file name, Equations is the equation system solved, Features lists the right-hand-side code paths the case exercises, and this column uses the following abbreviations:\n\nAbbreviation Meaning\nWF Weak form volume integral\nFD Flux differencing volume integral\nSC Shock capturing volume integral\n-nc With nonconservative terms (e.g. FD-nc, BC-nc)\nBC Non-periodic boundary conditions\nM Mortars\nSrc Source terms\n\nDegrees / Levels gives the default polynomial degree and initial refinement level used in CI benchmark runs. These match the values in the original Trixi.jl or TrixiShallowWater.jl examples.","title":"Cases by Dimension"},{"category":"section","location":"#1D-(13-cases)","page":"Home","text":"Case Equations Features Degrees / Levels\nadvection_basic Linear advection WF 3 / 4\nhypdiff_nonperiodic Hyperbolic diffusion WF, BC, Src 4 / 3\neuler_ec Compressible Euler FD 3 / 5\nmhd_ec Ideal GLM-MHD FD 3 / 4\nmhd_alfven_wave Ideal GLM-MHD FD 4 / 2\nshallowwater_ec Shallow water FD-nc 4 / 4\nshallowwater_source_terms Shallow water FD-nc, Src 3 / 3\neuler_quasi_source_terms_dirichlet Quasi compressible Euler FD-nc, BC-nc, Src 4 / 4\neuler_shock Compressible Euler SC 3 / 5\neuler_blast_wave Compressible Euler SC 3 / 6\nmhd_briowu_shock_tube Ideal GLM-MHD SC, BC 4 / 4\neuler_quasi_discontinuous Quasi compressible Euler SC-nc 3 / 6\nshallowwater_shock_capturing Shallow water SC-nc, BC-nc 4 / 3","title":"1D (13 cases)"},{"category":"section","location":"#2D-(13-cases)","page":"Home","text":"Case Equations Features Degrees / Levels\nadvection_basic Linear advection WF 3 / 4\neuler_source_terms_nonperiodic Compressible Euler WF, BC, Src 3 / 4\nhypdiff_nonperiodic Hyperbolic diffusion WF, BC, Src 4 / 3\neuler_ec Compressible Euler FD 3 / 5\neuler_vortex_mortar_split Compressible Euler FD, M 3 / 4\nmhd_alfven_wave_dirichlet Ideal GLM-MHD FD-nc, BC-nc 3 / 4\nmhd_alfven_wave_mortar Ideal GLM-MHD FD-nc, M-nc 3 / 4\nshallowwater_source_terms Shallow water FD-nc, Src 3 / 3\neuler_shock Compressible Euler SC 3 / 5\neuler_sedov_blast_wave Compressible Euler SC 3 / 6\neuler_blob_mortar Compressible Euler SC, M 3 / 4\nmhd_orszag_tang Ideal GLM-MHD SC-nc 3 / 4\nmhd_rotor Ideal GLM-MHD SC-nc 4 / 4","title":"2D (13 cases)"},{"category":"section","location":"#3D-(11-cases)","page":"Home","text":"Case Equations Features Degrees / Levels\nhypdiff_nonperiodic Hyperbolic diffusion WF, BC, Src 4 / 2\nadvection_mortar Linear advection WF, M 3 / 2\neuler_mortar Compressible Euler WF, M, Src 3 / 2\neuler_ec Compressible Euler FD 3 / 3\neuler_taylor_green_vortex Compressible Euler FD 3 / 3\nmhd_alfven_wave Ideal GLM-MHD FD-nc 3 / 2\nmhd_ec Ideal GLM-MHD FD-nc 3 / 2\nmhd_alfven_wave_mortar Ideal GLM-MHD FD-nc, M-nc 3 / 2\neuler_shock Compressible Euler SC 3 / 3\neuler_sedov_blast_wave Compressible Euler SC, BC 3 / 2\nmhd_ec_shockcapturing Ideal GLM-MHD SC-nc 4 / 3","title":"3D (11 cases)"}]
